    "text": "By WTVG Staff ,\n4 hours ago TOLEDO, Ohio (WTVG) - A boarded-up building in Toledo is set to be demolished Wednesday night after a fire broke out inside. The flames started in the building on the 2500 block of Albion Street, near Kress Street, around 7 p.m. Firefighters responded and were able to contain it. Nobody was hurt. Read full article",
